    iommu: arm-smmu: add global register definitions used by the QSMMU
    
    Original integration rationale and historical observations follow. These
    observations do not qualify hardware on this refreshed base.
    
    The MSM8974 QSMMU support about to be added to qcom_iommu has to program
    the SMMU global register space itself, and several of the architectural
    registers and fields it needs are missing from arm-smmu.h: the secure
    configuration and fault registers sCR2, sGFAR and sGFSRRESTORE, the sCR0
    SMCFCFG and STALLD fields and the S2CR NSCFG and MEMATTR fields.
    
    Add them, sorted by their register offset and bit positions.
    
    Original integration AI credit: Claude:claude-fable-5.
    
    Refreshed from integration source
    772813c92b768086cad84c34642ace7f9d6068c3. Current-base adaptation and
    host qualification used OpenAI Codex. Human review and new DCO
    certification remain pending.

